+\noindent\textbf{Time.} A bound counts the transitions named in its model. Communication, checking, waiting, and handover are included when they consume that time. An administrative act is not free merely because it changes a record rather than performing ordinary service.
+
+\noindent\textbf{Probability.} Almost-sure completion permits exceptional paths of probability zero. Sure completion covers every declared path. The distinction is essential in the service and stopping results.
+
+\noindent\textbf{Authority.} A permission is an operational relation within a stipulated authorization system, not a conclusion about moral worth or a statement of current law. A truthful record, a valid proof, and an authorized act answer different questions.
+
+\noindent\textbf{Resources.} Execution slots, monetary transfers, information access, and accepted obligations retain their own units. The theory does not silently exchange them or duplicate them when software is copied.
